B.a9D=s(["The second part of the test: 14 video clips of everyday road scenes, filmed from a car.","Each clip has at least one developing hazard; one clip has two. A developing hazard is something that would make you change speed or direction.","Click as soon as you see it starting to develop. The earlier you respond, the more points: up to 5 for each hazard.","Clicking all the time or in a pattern scores 0 for that clip.","You cannot go back or change your answer. The pass mark is 44 out of 75.","You take both parts at the same sitting, with up to a 3-minute break between them, and must pass both."],t.s)
